# card draws a Towers of Hanoi whose twelve disks are the lines of a
# Christmas message.  TRAPFREE is not optional, and the reason is the cio.l +
# clib.l collision described in rebuild.sh -- the SILENT form of it.
#
# Measured 2026-08-25, same source, same everything else:
#
#     -qixm  cio.l + clib.l          BUS ERROR ~40 moves in, at I$WritLn
#     -qxm   clib.l alone            runs to the end
#     -qm    clibn.l, stands alone   runs to the end
#
# Stack size makes no difference (16k and 64k fail identically), and neither
# does curses.l.  `cc -qixm' hands l68 BOTH cio.l and this SDK's clib.l, which
# is a FULL library -- for thirteen of 290 programs that produced a loud
# `caused name clashes' and the driver drops to -qxm.  card gets no such
# error: it links, and ends up with two stdio implementations, writing through
# a FILE that nothing initialised.  A duplicate-symbol failure is the loud
# version of what card does quietly.
#
# -qxm would also work and is smaller, but the driver only steps down to it
# after a link error, and -qxm still reaches math through a trap.  -qm stands
# alone, so card is not starred.
card|card|card.c|TRAPFREE||
